WEBVTT

00:00:01.950 --> 00:00:04.980
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the Supreme Monarch, Dande...

00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:10.110
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew...

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:15.850
This is the story of their lives and adventures.

00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:28.380
Whoa! What’s this?

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:31.240
You had this hidden talent
all along?!

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:32.350
Well, yeah.

00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:35.930
And I’m just about to set
a new personal record!

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:39.380
Wow!

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:42.100
Not like it’s any <i>use</i> to us, though.

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:49.210
It’s so loud in here, meow...

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:50.360
Nyarth?

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:53.860
I think I caught a cold, meow...

00:00:54.830 --> 00:00:57.890
I caught a cold, meow...

00:00:58.430 --> 00:00:59.740
Huh?

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:05.000
I said... I caught...
a cold, meow...

00:01:06.590 --> 00:01:08.700
No way! Did you catch a cold?

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:11.490
I’ve been trying to
tell you that, meow!

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:12.710
Huh?

00:01:12.710 --> 00:01:14.630
Never mind, meow.

00:01:14.630 --> 00:01:18.580
Kidding, kidding,
just kidding with ya. A Rocket Joke.

00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:21.560
If you’ve caught a cold,
you better keep warm.

00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:27.990
Health must come first,
or else evil can’t prosper.

00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:31.230
Musashi... Kojiro...

00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:34.640
Hey, are you thirsty?
Want anything to eat?

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:37.610
Some potato chips?
Or some canned Momon Berries?

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:42.490
Some nice and cool
ice cream’d be great... Oh!

00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:46.090
How about a hot pie
with cream and ice cream on top!

00:01:46.090 --> 00:01:47.460
Agreed!

00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:53.250
Aren’t you just suggesting treats
that you want yourselves, meow?

00:01:54.390 --> 00:02:00.290
You’re using my cold as an excuse
to try and slack off, meow...

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:03.060
No way!

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:06.360
You know, it’s like, it’s like...

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:08.650
You know?

00:02:09.510 --> 00:02:10.960
What do you mean
“You know,” meow?

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:15.420
You’re just trying to hide the fact
that you couldn’t think of anything, meow.

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:17.020
Oh, dear...

00:02:17.020 --> 00:02:20.060
You really need to get some rest.

00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:23.730
Come on, lie down.

00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:25.700
Hold on, meow.

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:34.590
I just realized the exact thing
that Team Rocket is lacking, meow!

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:36.380
What now?

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:38.510
Something we’re lacking?

00:02:39.190 --> 00:02:41.010
What could it be?!

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:42.600
It is...

00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:44.490
Gulp!

00:02:44.490 --> 00:02:47.340
To get right to the point, it is...

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:50.980
What?

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:53.160
He fell asleep?

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:54.940
That’s gonna gnaw at me!

00:02:54.940 --> 00:03:00.410
I <i>need</i> to know
what it is we’re lacking!

00:03:01.070 --> 00:03:02.680
...All done...

00:03:02.680 --> 00:03:04.570
He’s really fast asleep...

00:03:04.570 --> 00:03:05.200
Yeah.

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:08.610
So, what do we do now?

00:03:08.610 --> 00:03:09.950
Hmm...

00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:13.330
We were beaten by the brat boys
just yesterday...

00:03:14.710 --> 00:03:16.690
What’s that? A drone?

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:25.100
Pikachu?

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:28.930
Were you spying on Pikachu
with that drone?

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:31.810
What?! When?!

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:35.060
Did you see those fast turns?!

00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:39.820
Sure did. And he had like a
“Not even breaking a sweat” kinda face!

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:43.940
No wonder we’ve had a hard time catching him,
when he’s moving about like <i>that.</i>

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:47.290
Isn’t this it?

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:48.660
It has to be.

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:49.580
It’s decided!

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:54.980
Effective immediately, I’m calling an emergency meeting and
study group for Operation “Get Pikachu For Sure”!

00:03:54.980 --> 00:03:56.140
Yeah!

00:03:56.140 --> 00:03:58.030
We’ll study Sonansu’s footage,

00:03:58.030 --> 00:04:02.790
and thoroughly analyze Pikachu’s
emotions and thought patterns!

00:04:02.790 --> 00:04:10.860
Then, with full understanding of his mind,
we’ll be able to catch him without fail or fuss!

00:04:11.970 --> 00:04:12.640
This is amazing, isn’t it?

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:14.650
Wow! This is such a great idea!
Why didn’t we think of this before?
This is amazing, isn’t it?

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:15.010
Wow! This is such a great idea!
Why didn’t we think of this before?

00:04:15.010 --> 00:04:17.370
You’re being too loud...
I can’t sleep...
Wow! This is such a great idea!
Why didn’t we think of this before?

00:04:17.370 --> 00:04:19.530
You’re being too loud...
I can’t sleep...

00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:23.690
Oh, my gosh!
I think I’m a genius!

00:04:23.690 --> 00:04:27.330
Like, I just came up with the perfect way
to understand Pikachu!

00:04:27.730 --> 00:04:30.160
Really? What is it?

00:04:31.910 --> 00:04:33.080
Dubbing over him!

00:04:34.810 --> 00:04:37.250
Dubbing over him?

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:38.930
Indeed.

00:04:38.930 --> 00:04:42.630
Don’t you think we
rely on Nyarth too much?

00:04:42.630 --> 00:04:44.160
Meaning...?

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:46.020
Just think back.

00:04:46.020 --> 00:04:50.080
Everything Pikachu says,
we gotta have Nyarth translate.

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:51.370
You’re right!

00:04:51.370 --> 00:04:56.500
The days of Team Rocket depending
solely on Nyarth are over, right now!

00:04:56.500 --> 00:05:02.000
After today’s meeting,
we’ll be able to understand Pikachu’s speech!

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:04.520
I see! That’s why
we’re dubbing over him!

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:05.940
Precisely!

00:05:06.490 --> 00:05:08.510
Dubbing over Pikachu?

00:05:08.510 --> 00:05:11.220
It’s not a bad approach, meow.

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:15.290
Though it’s kinda sad to think
I won’t be needed anymore.

00:05:15.290 --> 00:05:18.010
Hey! Hey! Nyarth! Wake up!

00:05:18.010 --> 00:05:19.790
We’re gonna dub over Pikachu!

00:05:19.790 --> 00:05:22.580
So come and judge
if we get it right!

00:05:22.580 --> 00:05:26.340
You’re gonna lean
<i>entirely</i> on me?!

00:05:26.750 --> 00:05:28.960
Huh? He seems pretty energetic?

00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:33.820
Because I just <i>had</i> to
shout back at that one, meow...

00:05:34.350 --> 00:05:37.200
Ah... He fell asleep again.

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:40.140
He must’ve used up his energy
by forcing himself to shout.

00:05:40.140 --> 00:05:43.440
Then we’ll just have to
study without him.

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:44.480
Yeah.

00:05:44.480 --> 00:05:48.080
All right!
Sonansu, roll the footage!

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:50.390
I’ll have the first go.

00:05:57.080 --> 00:05:57.920
Okay.

00:05:58.280 --> 00:06:00.150
Ha! Hahaha-ha!

00:06:00.150 --> 00:06:04.980
See? You can’t catch up to Pockun!
Dumb and dim human child!

00:06:04.980 --> 00:06:06.300
Cut! Cut!

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:08.470
What? Don’t interrupt me.

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:11.590
No way! Even I could tell.

00:06:11.590 --> 00:06:14.000
You don’t understand
Pikachu’s feelings at all!

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:14.930
Huh?

00:06:14.930 --> 00:06:17.070
First, what’s “Pockun”?!

00:06:17.070 --> 00:06:20.690
Huh? Pikachu calls himself
Pockun, right?

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:23.690
No, he doesn’t! Full stop!

00:06:23.690 --> 00:06:25.920
And what’s with “human child”?!

00:06:25.920 --> 00:06:28.570
You know I meant the brat boy!

00:06:28.940 --> 00:06:30.970
I asked because I had no idea!

00:06:30.970 --> 00:06:34.740
Also, Musashi, your inner Pikachu’s
super pompous!

00:06:34.740 --> 00:06:37.710
Huh? Your inner Pikachu isn’t?

00:06:37.710 --> 00:06:39.760
No, he isn’t!

00:06:39.760 --> 00:06:42.940
He’s, well...

00:06:42.940 --> 00:06:44.500
Definitely not pompous, at least!

00:06:45.330 --> 00:06:50.720
What’s your problem?
If you’re so confident, Kojiro, then <i>you</i> try it!

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:52.920
Oh... Sure.

00:06:52.920 --> 00:06:54.800
Then I’ll have a go.

00:06:54.800 --> 00:06:56.340
Sonansu, go ahead.

00:06:56.340 --> 00:06:57.850
Ahh. Ahh.

00:06:59.130 --> 00:06:59.730
Okay.

00:07:02.840 --> 00:07:06.620
Hah... Pi finally have some time
to piself, pi.

00:07:06.620 --> 00:07:09.160
Freedom is just the best, pi.

00:07:09.160 --> 00:07:13.230
But still, pi’s calves
are aching again today, pi.

00:07:13.230 --> 00:07:17.470
Being on Satoshi’s shoulder
for ages is hard, pi.

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:20.860
But Satoshi’s doing his best
to carry pi too, pi.

00:07:20.860 --> 00:07:24.130
Pi want to reward him for that, pi!

00:07:24.130 --> 00:07:28.010
Ah... Pi wonder if there’s
any good massage parlors around, pi...

00:07:28.010 --> 00:07:29.590
Cut!

00:07:29.590 --> 00:07:32.530
What’s wrong?
I just got to a good part...

00:07:32.530 --> 00:07:33.590
A good part?

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:38.140
I perfectly synced with Pikachu’s feelings,
don’t you think?

00:07:38.140 --> 00:07:40.230
You did?!

00:07:40.230 --> 00:07:43.950
Why does he end
his sentences with “pi”?!

00:07:43.950 --> 00:07:46.860
I must’ve fallen asleep, meow.

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:53.110
Well, “Pi” “ka” “ch” “u”.
The cutest sound is “pi”, right?

00:07:53.110 --> 00:07:56.850
So, I thought
he’d end his sentences with “pi.”

00:07:56.850 --> 00:07:58.770
Yeah, “pi” is cute.

00:07:58.770 --> 00:07:59.500
See?

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:03.360
So for argument’s sake,
let’s say he <i>does</i> end his sentences with “pi.”

00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:06.300
But then keep that
to the <i>end</i> of the sentence!

00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:09.510
You put loads of “pi”s
all over his speech!

00:08:11.130 --> 00:08:12.800
What are you talking about?

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:17.200
Those “pi”s are his first-person pronouns,
like “I” or “me”...

00:08:17.200 --> 00:08:20.520
That’s too confusing!
A pronoun like that’s way too confusing!

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:20.990
Really?

00:08:20.990 --> 00:08:21.850
That isn’t even what
I want to retort, meow...
Really?

00:08:21.850 --> 00:08:24.130
Of course!
That isn’t even what
I want to retort, meow...

00:08:24.130 --> 00:08:27.400
The point I want to retort is...

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:28.900
Okay, got it.

00:08:28.900 --> 00:08:33.150
Next time, let’s analyze
the video carefully first.

00:08:33.150 --> 00:08:34.160
Analyze it?

00:08:34.160 --> 00:08:35.250
Yeah.

00:08:35.250 --> 00:08:39.890
Sonansu, do you have any footage
with a close-up view of Pikachu’s face?

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:43.820
What an awful feeling!

00:08:44.420 --> 00:08:47.890
That’s just us blasting off!

00:08:47.890 --> 00:08:49.130
Not that, some Pikachu—

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:50.800
Hold on, Musashi.

00:08:55.260 --> 00:08:59.410
The drone camera
stayed with Pikachu?

00:08:59.410 --> 00:09:00.260
Looks like it.

00:09:04.680 --> 00:09:05.650
Hear that?

00:09:05.650 --> 00:09:06.640
I heard it.

00:09:06.640 --> 00:09:07.890
He said something.

00:09:07.890 --> 00:09:11.570
Talking to us as we blast off?

00:09:11.570 --> 00:09:13.000
I think so.

00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:14.010
Rewind.

00:09:15.770 --> 00:09:19.280
Oh, stop there.
Pause it, Sonansu.

00:09:21.950 --> 00:09:26.440
W-What? That expression...
It looks so kind.

00:09:26.440 --> 00:09:28.070
Yeah. Yeah!

00:09:28.070 --> 00:09:36.300
I never knew that after we blasted off,
he watched us with such a pure gaze.

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:40.170
Now I feel like I can dub him perfectly!

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:44.310
I bid you well.

00:09:44.310 --> 00:09:46.170
Pikachu’s so nice!

00:09:46.170 --> 00:09:48.440
Hold on! Maybe it’s...

00:09:50.080 --> 00:09:51.320
See ya soon!

00:09:51.320 --> 00:09:55.770
Oh, my! No way!
He’s actually waiting to see us?!

00:09:55.770 --> 00:09:57.830
He counts on us...!

00:09:57.830 --> 00:10:00.160
No, it could be...

00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:02.450
I love you!

00:10:02.450 --> 00:10:04.170
I love you, too!

00:10:04.170 --> 00:10:05.910
Me too!

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:10.460
What am I gonna do?! I don’t know how I should act
the next time I see Pikachu now!

00:10:10.460 --> 00:10:12.210
I can’t tell them.

00:10:12.210 --> 00:10:16.050
I can’t tell them what
Pikachu’s really saying.

00:10:16.050 --> 00:10:18.860
I can’t possibly tell them, meow...

00:10:18.860 --> 00:10:21.970
I can’t bear the fact that
we still have to try and catch him!

00:10:25.510 --> 00:10:28.190
Vending, come on!

00:10:30.040 --> 00:10:31.860
You up for it, Nyarth?

00:10:31.860 --> 00:10:36.050
Meow! I slept for half a day
and now I’m a hundred times better, meow!

00:10:36.050 --> 00:10:37.530
All right!

00:10:38.780 --> 00:10:39.990
Rocket!

00:10:39.990 --> 00:10:40.740
Vending!

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:42.610
Secret!

00:10:46.300 --> 00:10:48.070
Direct from Team Rocket HQ...

00:10:48.070 --> 00:10:50.450
Come on out, awesome Pokémon!

00:10:55.270 --> 00:10:56.170
Nod, nod.

00:10:56.170 --> 00:10:58.320
What does it say, meow?

00:10:58.320 --> 00:11:00.550
Today’s episode is a double-feature.

00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:04.520
That again, meow?!
What’re the titles, meow?

00:11:04.520 --> 00:11:06.540
“Half a Numacraw”, and...

00:11:06.540 --> 00:11:08.660
“Operation: Dub Pikachu!”...

00:11:09.290 --> 00:11:12.060
<i>“Operation: Dub Pikachu”?!</i>

00:11:12.060 --> 00:11:13.440
Does that mean...

00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:17.870
Our dubbing earlier
was the first episode?!

00:11:18.940 --> 00:11:20.330
No way.

00:11:21.450 --> 00:11:23.510
What’s going on?

00:11:35.140 --> 00:11:38.940
After this, it’s
“Half a Numacraw”, meow!

00:13:32.110 --> 00:13:33.620
The weather’s so nice!

00:13:33.620 --> 00:13:36.620
After all the rainy days lately...

00:13:37.310 --> 00:13:38.250
It feels great!

00:13:52.920 --> 00:13:54.060
Nu...

00:13:55.090 --> 00:13:56.180
Nu...

00:13:58.190 --> 00:14:02.440
Numacraw’s buried
in the ground!

00:14:03.560 --> 00:14:05.400
Pocket Monsters!

00:14:15.270 --> 00:14:19.590
Numacraw! Mud Fish Pokémon!
Water/Ground type!

00:14:19.590 --> 00:14:25.830
Because it weakens if its skin dries out,
it replenishes fluids by playing in mud!

00:14:25.830 --> 00:14:27.220
Which means...

00:14:27.220 --> 00:14:30.220
Isn’t this pretty dangerous for it?

00:14:33.660 --> 00:14:34.520
It’s no good.

00:14:34.520 --> 00:14:36.660
It’s set hard.

00:14:39.420 --> 00:14:41.220
And I can’t grab it...

00:14:42.210 --> 00:14:44.780
How did it let this happen?

00:14:44.780 --> 00:14:46.580
Was it asleep or something?

00:14:47.450 --> 00:14:49.920
Anyway, we better get it out quick.

00:14:51.750 --> 00:14:53.120
If I catch it...!

00:14:53.120 --> 00:14:54.290
That’s it!

00:14:54.290 --> 00:14:56.660
Monster Ball...!

00:14:57.430 --> 00:14:59.180
Go...

00:15:05.300 --> 00:15:07.300
What?!

00:15:08.790 --> 00:15:13.920
Then... How about loosening up
the dirt with some water?

00:15:13.920 --> 00:15:15.450
Yeah! Let’s try it.

00:15:15.450 --> 00:15:17.560
But with what water?

00:15:21.560 --> 00:15:23.870
A row of Numacraw...

00:15:23.870 --> 00:15:24.570
Its friends?

00:15:28.070 --> 00:15:30.890
They’ve got a really
pleading look in their eyes...

00:15:30.890 --> 00:15:33.670
Then we can have them
use Water Gun!

00:15:33.670 --> 00:15:34.770
I get it!

00:15:34.770 --> 00:15:36.660
Hey! Numacraw!

00:15:38.180 --> 00:15:41.120
Huh? Hey, come over here...

00:15:43.530 --> 00:15:47.100
Satoshi!
It looks like they’re wary of us.

00:15:47.100 --> 00:15:47.750
Huh?

00:15:50.130 --> 00:15:54.310
But they’re worried
about their buried friend, huh...?

00:15:56.250 --> 00:15:58.170
Then how about Messon?

00:15:58.170 --> 00:16:00.020
Right! Go for it, Messon!

00:16:00.780 --> 00:16:02.350
Rescue it with Water Gun!

00:16:02.350 --> 00:16:04.850
Yeah! Give it a big soak!

00:16:25.640 --> 00:16:26.420
Huh?

00:16:26.420 --> 00:16:28.290
Why’d you vanish?!

00:16:28.290 --> 00:16:30.450
Messon! Where are you?

00:16:35.890 --> 00:16:36.970
All right...

00:16:37.770 --> 00:16:42.890
Let’s carry this water to Numacraw
like a bucket relay!

00:16:44.580 --> 00:16:45.650
Okay!

00:16:47.150 --> 00:16:48.920
Go on, Rabbifoot!

00:17:00.910 --> 00:17:03.910
Looking good, Pikachu!
Keep going!

00:17:13.300 --> 00:17:16.130
Safe! You did great, Pikachu!

00:17:16.510 --> 00:17:18.350
You can leave the rest to me!

00:17:27.100 --> 00:17:30.470
Is there any other
way to do it...?

00:17:30.470 --> 00:17:33.010
Oh! I just came up with
a good idea!

00:17:33.010 --> 00:17:33.860
Really?

00:17:34.710 --> 00:17:36.360
See? If I...

00:17:42.540 --> 00:17:43.260
What?

00:17:45.980 --> 00:17:49.700
Are you trying to say
you’re gonna carry the water in your mouth?

00:17:49.700 --> 00:17:51.010
Yeah!

00:17:51.010 --> 00:17:52.120
Ah!

00:17:53.320 --> 00:17:55.070
Maybe that won’t work either...

00:17:55.070 --> 00:17:55.630
Probably not.

00:18:07.530 --> 00:18:08.440
What happened?

00:18:08.440 --> 00:18:11.320
Looks like it’s not doing too well...

00:18:12.340 --> 00:18:14.690
It might be getting weak...

00:18:14.690 --> 00:18:16.090
We need to save it quickly.

00:18:16.820 --> 00:18:19.450
But how...?!

00:18:26.200 --> 00:18:27.740
What’s that?

00:18:28.910 --> 00:18:33.170
Runpappa! Carefree Pokémon!
Water/Grass-type!

00:18:33.170 --> 00:18:38.470
Upon hearing an upbeat and cheerful rhythm,
the cells in its body become active!

00:18:45.400 --> 00:18:48.830
Runpappa! Use Rain Prayer!
Rain-Pra-yer!

00:18:49.490 --> 00:18:51.190
Please! Runpappa!

00:18:54.070 --> 00:18:56.880
Rain Prayer!
Rain-Pra-yer!

00:18:56.880 --> 00:19:00.610
Bring rain and loosen up the dirt!

00:19:06.620 --> 00:19:08.410
Looks like it understood us!

00:19:08.410 --> 00:19:09.670
All right!

00:19:19.550 --> 00:19:20.910
Yeah, that’s it!

00:19:20.910 --> 00:19:23.180
This sunshine is
just what we needed!

00:19:25.180 --> 00:19:28.230
Wait, that was Clear Skies!

00:19:29.020 --> 00:19:32.610
No! What we want is Rain Prayer!

00:19:34.610 --> 00:19:36.270
It didn’t understand at all.

00:19:36.270 --> 00:19:39.490
Please!
We want to save Numacraw!

00:19:43.160 --> 00:19:44.940
We’re not getting through to it...

00:20:32.040 --> 00:20:34.170
It worked!

00:21:07.280 --> 00:21:09.530
Glad you’re safe, Numacraw!

00:21:09.530 --> 00:21:12.900
Don’t get buried again, okay?

00:21:33.230 --> 00:21:35.890
Nu...

00:21:35.890 --> 00:21:41.070
Numacraw’s buried
in the ground!

00:21:41.070 --> 00:21:42.920
And there’s <i>more</i>
this time!

00:21:50.960 --> 00:21:51.730
